DOLLY 7
PACKAGE go
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
# go downloads modules with net/http, which records http@0.
REQUIRES HOST http@0

# The Go toolchain as go-build built it, in its GOROOT. The commands start it
# by its own path, from which it finds its GOROOT.
FROM /v0.1.4/demos/go/Dollyfile-go-build f7f447b2cc2d22bd7cdb740f712d683b77500b28f467e11b10ffd93bb7984606
FILE /usr/bin/go
    #!/bin/slop
    /usr/lib/go/bin/go "$@"
FILE /usr/bin/gofmt
    #!/bin/slop
    /usr/lib/go/bin/gofmt "$@"
EXPORTS TOOL go
EXPORTS TOOL gofmt
# go.env's GOTOOLCHAIN=auto would fetch newer toolchains, which do not run here.
EXPORTS ENV GOTOOLCHAIN local
EXPORTS FOLDER go-root /usr/lib/go
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/go.1
    go: the Go toolchain (Go 1.27.3) for GOOS=dolly GOARCH=wasm64, built inside
    Dolly from its pinned sources.
    
      go build              compiles a package and its dependencies
      go run main.go        compiles and runs a program
      gofmt -l .            lists files whose formatting differs
    
    Programs are pure Go: there is no cgo, and they run single-threaded.
    net/http goes through the page's HTTP broker (its policy, and CORS), so
    go get works with proxy.golang.org; net's sockets reach nothing.
    signal.Notify receives the kernel's signals; syscall.Exec replaces the
    program. Upstream's documentation: https://go.dev/doc/
